{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 EXIT — root cause confirmed, mechanism and legitimacy both proven\n\n### Root cause (a changeable artifact)\n\nThe mcp image never contains git metadata, so no attested gate can resolve a ref:\n\n- `.dockerignore:5` excludes `.git`.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:42` is `COPY . /app`, with `WORKDIR /app` at `:33`.\n\nSo `/app` is a plain source copy. `_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:293` raises\n`cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'` because there is no repository to\nresolve against.\n\n### Runtime proof (dynamic claim, observed executing — not read from source)\n\n    docker exec compose-mcp-1 sh -c 'ls -d /app/.git; cat /app/.deployed_ref; echo $REBAR_ROOT; pwd'\n      ls: cannot access '/app/.git': No such file or directory\n      d4a0a2a44 (feat/gerrit-ci-verified-gate)\n      REBAR_ROOT=[<unset>]\n      /app\n\n`.deployed_ref` is a TEXT MARKER standing in for a clone. `REBAR_ROOT` is unset, so the repo\nroot resolves to the working directory `/app`, which has no `.git`. That is the whole\nmechanism: every attested-source gate (`review_plan`, `verify_completion`, `review_code`,\n`reconcile`) fails identically, and `attach_commits` can resolve no SHA.\n\n**Discriminating detail:** `source: \"local\"` DOES run — which rules out \"the gates are broken\"\nand isolates the fault to the attested-source path specifically, i.e. to the missing repo\nrather than to the gate code. But a local verdict is never signed, so it cannot satisfy a gate.\n\n### Legitimacy: incomplete-implementation (NOT feature-request)\n\nCited design authority — **ADR 0104 §3**:\n\n> For the two op-cert kinds minted via MCP (plan-review at claim, completion-verifier at close\n> — ADR 0049) to be **enforceable**, the MCP server signs them under the box's **EXISTING**\n> opcert signing environment...\n\nThe capability was designed and approved with an operator ruling (2026-08-24, Option A). It was\nnever wired: the service shipped without a repo for the attested source to resolve against.\nThat is a defect-class miss, not a feature request.\n\n### Net effect\n\nNo attestation can be earned through the live MCP server, so no task/story/epic can be closed\nthrough it without a force — which agents are forbidden to use. The MCP surface is therefore\nunable to complete the very workflow AGENTS.md directs agents to route through it.\n\n### Attribution — by SCOPE OF WORK, not by introducing commit\n\nNo commit broke this; the service never had a repo, so `git blame` has nothing to find. The\nscope-of-work owner is **`fd4a-4e91-f179-4932`** (`cibophobic-holohedral-esok`,\n\"rebar-mcp HTTP transport service on the AWS box\"), the story that shipped the service and\nits Dockerfile. A reviewer of that story could plausibly have caught that a container with no\n`.git` cannot serve certified ops the ADR says it must — which is the test for a correct\nattribution target. Recorded here because the `caused_by` link form is gated on the target\nhaving a referencing commit and this is an omission."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787851646659272001,"uuid":"0ddab002-8156-4579-b13d-197e5217ea38"}